The attached image, Fig. 4, illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are actively transported to the draining lymph nodes and taken up by antigen-presenting cells (APCs). Flow cytometry analysis over 7 days shows a peak percentage of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells in the lymph node on Day 2. Nano-11 is predominantly found in migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) and, to a lesser extent, in monocytes/macrophages and lymphoid tissue resident DCs. MigDCs also exhibit the highest mean fluorescence intensity, indicating greater per-cell uptake of Nano-11, highlighting their key role in adjuvant delivery.